  "body": "<!-- ⚠️ If you do not respect this template, your issue will be closed -->\r\n<!-- ⚠️ Make sure to browse the opened and closed issues to confirm this idea does not exist. -->\r\n\r\n### What is the expected enhancement?\r\nMany optimization objects, e.g. `Constraint`, `Variable` do not have textual representations, e.g. methods like `__str__` and `__repr__` and in a debugger, e.g. PyCharm they don't provide much information out of box. `QuadraticProgram` has only `__repr__` which, in turns, depends on the docplex implementation, and in the debugger you can only see a docplex comment header of the LP representation.\r\n\r\nThis issue should be fixed by reviewing optimization objects and introducing textual representation methods in them. \r\n\r\n",
